# PROTOTYPE — injection template, runs INSIDE the living target instance (clone-and-run).
# Tests whether an expression's call chain can be evaluated WITHOUT a runtime error.
# Why: in frameworks a chain like MoContext.$mdManagerWindow().$commandController().$activateTarget
# can resolve a MIDDLE term to 'unnamed_value', and the NEXT term then causes a HARD runtime error.
# $cando never errors, so we walk the chain term by term and $cando-test each growing prefix —
# always WITHOUT the trailing brackets, so the methods are never executed (no evaluation, no side
# effects). Returns kTrue only if every prefix is valid → the caller may then evaluate the whole
# chain safely.
# WARNING: when the caller finally evaluates the chain, the intermediate links with '()' are
# EXECUTED to navigate to the next reference (e.g. $commandController() in
# MoContext.$mdManagerWindow().$commandController().$activateTarget). A link with side effects
# (...$giveRefAndDeleteData()...) would then alter data. This $cando test itself never executes
# them — it tests each prefix WITHOUT the trailing brackets.

Calculate rest as pExpr ## strtok consumes a copy of this, term by term
Calculate prefix as '' ## the growing path tested so far

While len(rest)
	# append the next term ('.' separated) to the prefix
	Calculate prefix as con(prefix,pick(len(prefix)=0,'.',''),strtok('rest','.')) ## strtok needs a literal var name
	
	# build the test prefix WITHOUT the trailing bracket pair, so $cando does not execute it.
	# scan from the end, balancing, to drop the last (...) whatever it contains, e.g. $do('a.b') or $do(x(y))
	Calculate testExpr as prefix
	If mid(testExpr,len(testExpr),1)=')'
		Calculate level as 0
		Calculate scanPos as len(testExpr)
		While scanPos>0
			If mid(testExpr,scanPos,1)=')'
				Calculate level as level+1
			Else If mid(testExpr,scanPos,1)='('
				Calculate level as level-1
				If level=0
					Calculate testExpr as mid(testExpr,1,scanPos-1) ## cut the trailing call
					Break to end of loop
				End If
			End If
			Calculate scanPos as scanPos-1
		End While
	End If
	
	If not([testExpr].$cando) ## this term cannot be evaluated here → chain is unsafe / does not resolve
		Quit method kFalse
	End If
End While

Quit method kTrue